            <title>[LU-21172] lod: lod_ost_alloc_qos() on-stack timer is not set up with timer_setup_on_stack()</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21172</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Problem"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Problem&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On a kernel with CONFIG_DEBUG_OBJECTS_TIMERS, recovery-small test_152 prints this warning on the MDS (3 times, in thread mdt00_001):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;ODEBUG: object ... is on stack ..., but NOT annotated.
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Cause"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Cause&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;lod_ost_alloc_qos() puts "struct semaphore_timer timer" on the stack when down_write_trylock(lq_rw_sem) fails, then sets it up with timer_setup(). Debug objects expects a timer on the stack to be set up with timer_setup_on_stack() and released with destroy_timer_on_stack(). This code came with &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-15393" title="object allocation when OST is lost" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-15393"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-15393&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (f46782b4c7).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There is no harm on a normal kernel; the test still passes. It is only noise on a debug kernel.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Possiblefix"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Possible fix&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;timer_setup_on_stack(&amp;amp;timer.timer, process_semaphore_timer, 0);
...
timer_delete_sync(&amp;amp;timer.timer);
destroy_timer_on_stack(&amp;amp;timer.timer);
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Environment"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Environment&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Found on a 2.17.57-based build, single node, Rocky 9.8 debug kernel (5.14.0-687 with KASAN, lockdep and debug objects). The code is the same in master (2.17.61).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
