                            <comment id="505695" author="JIRAUSER21604" created="Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:27:19 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Fixed on master by &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-8933" title="sanity test_51d: object distribution between OSTs not even" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-8933"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-8933&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (commit aa26e45f67, "lod: leave inactive targets out of the RR array"). That patch moved the timed down_write() in lod_ost_alloc_qos() into a new helper, lu_down_write_timeout() in lustre/obdclass/lu_tgt_alloc.c. The helper uses timer_setup_on_stack() and timer_destroy_on_stack(), so the ODEBUG warning is gone. No on-stack timer is left in lustre/lod. My patch &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/70653" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/70653&lt;/a&gt; is abandoned.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
